 procedure (36 total)\", and the five numbered category rows carry 12 + 6 + 6 + 9 + 3 = 36. The number 36 is correct; the noun attached to it is not. Say \"36 services\" or \"36 defined services across 5 categories\" — do not say \"36 service categories\", \"36 defined service categories\" or \"36 specific service categories\". Registered facts: CMA-DRAFT-PRICE-LIST-SERVICES-36 and CMA-DRAFT-PRICE-LIST-CATEGORIES-5."], "current_value": "The served page as at 2026-09-04. Each correction above names the exact wrong wording and the exact right wording. Everything not named is correct and must not be touched.", "suggestion": "Apply ONLY the corrections listed in `corrections`, in place, keeping each sentence''s surrounding structure. These are factual corrections to regulatory claims on a site whose readers are pet owners and veterinary practices deciding what the law requires of them.", "constraint": "SMALLEST TRUE CHANGE. This is a CORRECTION, not a rewrite — the risk here is a wholesale regeneration, not an insufficient edit. Change ONLY the sentences named above. Do NOT rewrite, reorder, condense or improve any other prose on the page. Do NOT introduce any figure, statistic, date, example or named source that is not already an evidenced fact in this site''s evidence_base register (migration 759, 21 facts) — that register is the CLOSED SET of figures this site may assert. Do NOT add independence claims about this site, do NOT add practice prices, and do NOT use the phrase \"proprietary data\" (all four are banned_claims patterns on this site, and the third and fourth are what it was remediated for in July 2026). Leave everything else byte-identical.", "affected_component": "Page body — the sentences named in `corrections`", "acceptance_test": "Fetch https://vetcomparison.uk/guides/tool-cma-obligation-checker-guide.html and confirm: \"£21\" and \"£12.50\" must STILL be present (the figures stay) AND the page must now say the cap is proposed/draft rather than in force 