 within the same sentence; \"service categories\" must be GONE (count 0 for \"36 service categories\", \"36 defined service categories\" and \"36 specific service categories\") while \"36\" remains. Then diff the visible text against the pre-edit version: the ORPHANED-SENTENCE count must be 0 — that is, no sentence may vanish without a close survivor. (Do NOT use the stricter \"no sentence reworded\" test: a correction necessarily rewords the sentence it corrects. Measured on the loancash restoration 2026-09-03, 5 sentences were reworded at 0.89-0.98 similarity with 0 orphaned.) Use an invented-URL 404 as a fetch control. No verifier is registered for content_rewrite, so a ''complete'' status is NOT evidence — verify at the bytes.", "authority": "OWNER INSTRUCTION 2026-09-04: ''please fix the vetcomparison copy''. The three errors were found and recorded (not repaired) by the evidence-register pass of 2026-09-03, migration 759, as four corrects_site_citation entries. The site''s own lane was consulted before filing and confirmed nothing is mid-flight on these pages.", "beware": "A page_rerender re-ships stored content_data and completes successfully — it cannot correct anything. No verifier is registered for content_rewrite, so ''complete'' is not evidence the bytes changed. Verify at the served bytes with the acceptance_test above.", "do_not_touch": "/guides/animal-health-certificates/index.html is NOT in this set and must not be edited. Its article body is a HAND-ATTESTED LITERAL block (vetcomparison lane, D16-class correction of 2026-08-27, every sentence traced to a gov.uk fetch) that REPLACED three model-memory falsehoods. A regeneration there would reintroduce them. Measured 2026-09-04: that page carries 0 instances of all three errors, so it needs no repair.", "filed_by_lane": "bugfix_414 register-programme lane (migration 771)"}'::jsonb,
   (SELECT id  FROM pages WHERE site_id='72b9e3a6-872f-4528-a6d6-7f205ea60f4d' AND url='/how-it-works.html'),
   (SELECT url FROM pages WHERE site_id='72b9e3a6-872f-4528-a6d6-7f205ea60f4d' AND url='/how-it-works.html'),
   15, 'page-build-handler', 'triaged',
   'bugfix_414 register-programme lane (migration 771)', 'vetcomparison_fix_how_it_works', 'manual');

DO $$
DECLARE n int; nlive int; nahc int; nmanual int; nurl int;
BEGIN
  SELECT count(*) INTO n FROM site_work_items WHERE created_by = 'bugfix_414 register-programme lane (migration 771)';
  IF n IS DISTINCT FROM 9 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION '771 VERIFY: expected 9 repair items, found %', coalesce(n::text,'NULL');
  END IF;

  SELECT count(*) INTO nlive FROM site_work_items
   WHERE created_by = 'bugfix_414 register-programme lane (migration 771)' AND spec->>'mode' = 'edit_live'
     AND spec->>'constraint' LIKE '%SMALLEST TRUE CHANGE%'
     AND jsonb_array_length(spec->'corrections') >= 1;
  IF nlive IS DISTINCT FROM 9 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION '771 VERIFY: expected 9 items with mode=edit_live, the constraint and at least one correction, found %', coalesce(nlive::text,'NULL');
  END IF;

  -- guard 4: the hand-attested AHC page must NOT be in the set
  SELECT count(*) INTO nahc FROM site_work_items
   WHERE created_by = 'bugfix_414 register-programme lane (migration 771)' AND affected_url LIKE '%animal-health-certificates%';
  IF nahc IS DISTINCT FROM 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION '771 VERIFY: % item(s) target the hand-attested animal-health-certificates page - that page must never be regenerated', coalesce(nahc::text,'NULL');
  END IF;

  -- nothing may dispatch unreleased, and every affected_url must resolve to a real page of THIS site
  SELECT count(*) INTO nmanual FROM site_work_items WHERE created_by = 'bugfix_414 register-programme lane (migration 771)' AND approval_mode = 'manual' AND status = 'triaged';
  IF nmanual IS DISTINCT FROM 9 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION '771 VERIFY: expected 9 manual/triaged items, found %', coalesce(nmanual::text,'NULL');
  END IF;

  SELECT count(*) INTO nurl FROM site_work_items w JOIN pages p ON p.id = w.page_id
   WHERE w.created_by = 'bugfix_414 register-programme lane (migration 771)' AND w.affected_url = p.url AND p.site_id = '72b9e3a6-872f-4528-a6d6-7f205ea60f4d';
  IF nurl IS DISTINCT FROM 9 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION '771 VERIFY: only % of 9 items have a page_id/affected_url resolving to a vetcomparison page', coalesce(nurl::text,'NULL');
  END IF;

  RAISE NOTICE '771 OK: 9 correction items filed, all mode=edit_live and approval_mode=manual, AHC page excluded';
END $$;

COMMIT;
